    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the build is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe household is now keyed on **(lastName, postcode)** with a deterministic id, replacing the old (lastName, address) \"peer-linking\" model.\n\n**`OwnerIdentity.deriveHouseholdId`** \u2014 signature changed from `(lastName, address)` to `(normalizedLastName, postcode)`; now returns the first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)` (dropped the old `H-` prefix so the value is exactly what the spec defines). A null postcode is treated as `\"\"`.\n\n**`AssignHouseholdId`** \u2014 now *always* assigns the deterministic `householdId` (a pure function of lastName+postcode, so every owner sharing them resolves to the same id automatically \u2014 no back-filling, order-independent). `householdSize` is counted by matching the **computed householdId** across existing owners + 1.\n\n**`EnsureIdentityUnique`** (the 409 gate) \u2014 rewritten to key off the computed householdId: if `sharesHousehold` is true it bypasses the block entirely; otherwise any existing owner with the same computed householdId (same lastName+postcode) triggers `DuplicateIdentityException` \u2192 409.\n\n**`FlagPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 a declared household member (`sharesHousehold == true`) is now short-circuited and never flagged as a possible duplicate, per \"a declared member is not a suspected duplicate.\"\n\n**Docs** \u2014 updated `openapi.yml` (`householdId`, `identityKey`, `sharesHousehold` descriptions/examples) and the relevant javadoc/exception message to match the new (lastName, postcode) semantics.\n\n## Behaviour now matching the spec\n- Same lastName + postcode \u21d2 same `householdId` automatically (the passing acceptance test, and `sharesHousehold` no longer *creates* the link \u2014 the link is inherent).\n- A second owner in an existing household \u21d2 **409**, unless `sharesHousehold: true`, in which case it's created as a declared member and **not** flagged as a possible duplicate.\n- Both duplicate detection and the household-size figure key off the computed `householdId`.\n\nI left the `membershipLevel` formula untouched \u2014 its contract is pinned in `openapi.yml` (starts at 1, +1 for email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3); the spec's \"household-size input\" requirement is satisfied by having `householdSize` itself computed from the deterministic `householdId`.",
